      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Chessboard corner detection\n\nThe first step of camera calibration: locate the inner corners of a chessboard. \n'cv2.findChessboardCorners' returns the 9x6 grid of corners (plus a 'found' flag) and 'cv2.drawChessboardCorners' overlays the standard connected colour pattern. patternSize counts INNER corners per row/column, not squares. \nFeed several views into cv2.calibrateCamera to recover the intrinsics, or one view + cv2.solvePnP for the board's pose. \nNon-chessboard images yield found=false and pass through unmarked."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
